# Golden: Phase-7 node 9210 (Option-2 generated lead) -- "bossa" style, VarD
# peak section, a |C|F| two-bar change. Locks bossa's generated kLeadMotif
# (the new TrackRole::kLead pattern in bossa.hpp's kDP, no other section):
# seed=1202, length=6, center_degree=4 (the 5th), vel=64, gate=kGate8th,
# idiom_role=kDrums (onset candidates drawn from kDD's own side-stick/kick/
# closed-hat mask), gm_program=73 (Flute). Two full bars of VarD exercise BOTH
# halves of the call-and-response repeat policy (motif.hpp's apply_repeat):
# bar 1 (repeat=0, over C) plays the generated phrase verbatim -- the
# "statement" -- and bar 2 (repeat=1, over F) applies the seed's own
# kDiatonicTranspose with a repeat-keyed amount -- the "answer". Routes
# drums/bass/chord1 following arranger_band.acmd's own convention, plus
# `style route lead synth:7` -- WITHOUT this route the new kLead content never
# appears in the golden at all (the gap this fixture closes). Any accidental
# change to bossa's kLeadMotif or to kDD's onset mask moves these notes/ticks
# and fails this test.
key C major
port open out virt as synth
chord out synth:4
style load bossa
style route drums synth:10
style route bass synth:2
style route chord1 synth:3
style route lead synth:7
style section varD
seq new verse
seq add C 1bar
seq add F 1bar
seq loop on
seq play
transport start
advance 7680
quit
